---
permalink: /sitemap.xml
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#-
  Deliberately no <lastmod>, <changefreq> or <priority>.

  Google ignores changefreq and priority outright, and ignores lastmod
  unless it is consistently accurate. Eleventy's default page date is the
  source file's filesystem timestamp, which is the checkout time in a fresh
  clone - so every page would claim it was modified on the day the site was
  last built. Deriving it from git history instead cannot work either: the
  date of the commit carrying a change is not knowable while building the
  output that goes into that same commit.

  A sitemap of accurate <loc> values is worth more than one padded with
  metadata that is wrong. It also keeps the build reproducible, which is
  what scripts/check-docs-fresh.js relies on.
-#}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- for item in collections.all %}
{%- if not item.data.noindex %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ settings.url }}{{ item.url }}</loc>
  </url>
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
